    "question": "How do I check the PROS balance of an address on Pharos mainnet?",
    "docs": {
      "question": "How do I check the PROS balance of an address on Pharos mainnet?",
      "answer": "The quickest way is to open [Pharos Scan](https://www.pharosscan.xyz) and paste the address into its search bar. The address page shows its PROS balance and transaction history.\n\nFor a command-line check, query the Pharos mainnet RPC:\n\n```bash\ncurl https://rpc.pharos.xyz \\\n  -X POST \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n    \"method\": \"eth_getBalance\",\n    \"params\": [\"<address>\", \"latest\"],\n    \"id\": 1\n  }'\n```\n\nThe result is in wei. Divide it by `10^18` to get PROS. Pharos mainnet uses chain ID `1672`; see [Pacific Mainnet](https://docs.pharos.xyz/getting-started/network/pacific-mainnet) and [Get PROS Gas](https://docs.pharos.xyz/getting-started/get-pros-gas) for details.",
