    "question": "How do I find the USDC contract address on Pharos and read its total supply?",
    "docs": {
      "question": "How do I find the USDC contract address on Pharos and read its total supply?",
      "answer": "The address depends on which Pharos network you’re using. The [Token Registry](https://docs.pharos.xyz/getting-started/token-registry) lists:\n\n* **Pacific Mainnet:** USDC (Circle Deployed) — `0xc879c018db60520f4355c26ed1a6d572cdac1815`\n* **Atlantic Testnet:** USDC — `0xcfC8330f4BCAB529c625D12781b1C19466A9Fc8B`\n\nUse Foundry’s `cast call` to read `totalSupply()` without sending a transaction. For mainnet:\n\n```bash\nRPC=https://rpc.pharos.xyz\nTOKEN=0xc879c018db60520f4355c26ed1a6d572cdac1815\n\ncast call $TOKEN \"totalSupply()(uint256)\" --rpc-url $RPC\ncast call $TOKEN \"decimals()(uint8)\" --rpc-url $RPC\n```\n\nFor Atlantic Testnet, use its address and RPC instead:\n\n```bash\nRPC=https://atlantic.dplabs-internal.com\nTOKEN=0xcfC8330f4BCAB529c625D12781b1C19466A9Fc8B\n\ncast call $TOKEN \"totalSupply()(uint256)\" --rpc-url $RPC\ncast call $TOKEN \"decimals()(uint8)\" --rpc-url $RPC\n```\n\n`totalSupply()` returns the raw integer in base units. Divide it by `10^decimals` for the human-readable supply. The Atlantic registry lists USDC with **6 decimals**. The [Pharos Skill Engine](https://docs.pharos.xyz/tooling-and-infrastructure/pharos-skill-engine-guide) documents this `cast call` pattern.",
